course: dictionary
lesson: 15467
title: Stopped: ending, halting and blocking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «stopped» has three main meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Read the whole sentence first, then ask yourself what fits.
explain: «The rain stopped.» Here stopped means came to an end. «The bus stopped at the corner.» Here it means no longer moving. The same word has two different meanings, so the clues in each sentence decide which one is right.
explain: Sometimes stopped means blocked, as in «a stopped sink». To check, swap in your meaning: "The rain came to an end" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Stopped» is the past form of the verb stop, so it tells us something has already happened.
fact: «Stopped» can mean came to an end: «The rain stopped.»
fact: «Stopped» can mean no longer moving: «The bus stopped at the corner.»
fact: «Stopped» can mean blocked: «a stopped sink».
fact: «Stopped to» means paused to do something, and «stopped doing» means no longer did it.
exercise: «Suddenly the music stopped.» What does stopped mean here? | Started again | Blocked up | *Came to an end
exercise: «The car stopped at the red light, so we waited.» What does stopped mean? | Came to an end | *No longer moving | Blocked
exercise: «Ella stopped to tie her shoelace on the way to school.» What does stopped to mean? | Forgot to come to school | Ran very fast | *Paused to do something
test: «The rain stopped just before the picnic.» What does stopped mean? | Stuck to the grass | *Came to an end | Blocked up
test: «Ben stopped doing his homework when the bell rang.» What does stopped doing mean? | *No longer did it | Had just finished it | Started it again
exam: Which sentence uses stopped to mean blocked? | The rain stopped by lunch. | The bus stopped at the corner. | *The sink was stopped with leaves.
